From 04985f7de519f2c77b93acf4686d936d2a794df3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Strata layer <layer@studioz.local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:42:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] disk tier: archive (not delete) the parking copy in the three
 paths that discard it, opt-in

The compaction (discard_diverged), the supersede pass (drop_superseded) and the provisional park of a cancelled request destroy the state today. With --conversation-cache-archive-mode ids|state the copy is MOVED into <spill-dir>/archive instead of removed (off, the default, is byte-for-byte the previous behaviour). The archive has its own budget (--conversation-cache-archive-mib), its own GC (--conversation-cache-archive-keep, then the budget, plus optional --conversation-cache-archive-max-age-days) and is never a reuse candidate (best() cannot return one). The cancellation archives the PRE-revert state as the sidecar only (gate refinement a). A copy larger than the whole budget is not archived, and a failed MOVE (including mid-way in a multi-stage archive) leaves the tier entry intact (audit C8/O2/F3). Host-only tests: 287 checks.
